# XiaoWan Agent Enterprise

XiaoWan Agent Enterprise is a business-ready AI assistant built on top of the DeepSeek API. It includes:

- multi-model AI chat
- session-based conversation memory
- streaming responses in the browser
- markdown-formatted outputs
- export session data
- workbench-style dashboard
- optional ADB and local automation tooling
- optional authentication via environment variables
- Docker and one-click startup support

## Features

- DeepSeek Chat / Coder / Reasoner models
- enterprise dashboard with usage summaries
- conversation deletion and export
- secure UI login when `ADMIN_USERNAME` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` are configured
- ADB device inspection and local command execution via env flag
- one-command launch via `launch.sh`
- Docker Compose deployment example

## Quick Start

1. Clone the repo and open the project folder.
2. Create a virtual environment:

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
```

3. Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

4. Configure environment variables in your shell or `.env` file:

```bash
export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"
export DEEPSEEK_API_URL="https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions"
export ENABLE_LOCAL_AUTOMATION="true"
export ADMIN_USERNAME="admin"
export ADMIN_PASSWORD="your-password"
export SECRET_KEY="your-random-secret"
```

5. Launch the app:

```bash
python app.py
```

6. Open the dashboard:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:5000
```

## Optional Enterprise Security

Set the following environment variables to enable login:

```bash
export ADMIN_USERNAME="admin"
export ADMIN_PASSWORD="strong-password"
export SECRET_KEY="your-random-secret"
```

If both `ADMIN_USERNAME` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` are empty, the app runs in open mode.

## Local Automation and ADB

To enable local command execution and ADB functions, set:

```bash
export ENABLE_LOCAL_AUTOMATION="true"
```

This enables:

- `/api/tool/local/command`
- `/api/tool/adb/devices`
- `/api/tool/adb/command`

## Docker Compose

You can run the app with Docker Compose:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Example `docker-compose.yml`:

```yaml
services:
  xiaowan-agent:
    build: .
    ports:
      - "5000:5000"
    environment:
      DEEPSEEK_API_KEY: ${DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}
      DEEPSEEK_API_URL: ${DEEPSEEK_API_URL:-https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions}
      ENABLE_LOCAL_AUTOMATION: ${ENABLE_LOCAL_AUTOMATION:-false}
      ADMIN_USERNAME: ${ADMIN_USERNAME:-}
      ADMIN_PASSWORD: ${ADMIN_PASSWORD:-}
      SECRET_KEY: ${SECRET_KEY:-xiaowan-enterprise-secret-key}
```

## One-click Launch

```bash
chmod +x launch.sh
./launch.sh
```

## Files

- `app.py` — Flask server and API endpoints
- `templates/index.html` — enterprise UI
- `templates/login.html` — login page
- `requirements.txt` — Python dependencies
- `docker-compose.yml` — deployment example
- `launch.sh` — one-click local launcher
- `.env.example` — example environment configuration

## Notes

This version is designed for business use and local deployment, with a stronger UI, protected access, and more operational capabilities than the basic chat prototype.

